# Dialogue_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Narrative genres with interactive conversation systems (open_world_rpg).

## 2. This document owns
- Dialogue system structure: node trees, condition hooks, camera/audio slots.
- Tone & branching rules (how many options, when hubs loop, interruption policy).
- Variable conventions referenced by dialogue conditions.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Actual dialogue text and performances — Narrative_Script.
- Quest logic that dialogue gates — Quest_Design (dialogue only references).
- Character voice definitions — Character_Sheets / Bible.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. System overview / 2. Node grammar / 3. Conditions & variables / 4. Branching rules / 5. Presentation slots / 6. Localization notes / 7. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Dialogue vs Script: system and rules here; authored lines in the Script.
- A dialogue node may check a quest state; it must never mutate it directly.

## 6. Common audit rules
- No dangling node references; every choice leads somewhere.
- Condition variables are declared once in the conventions chapter.
